This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[ed: This is posted in lieu of azgor, who was absent when the
spontaneous deletion of ideas swept through.  This is also in
opposition to a non-serious post under the same subject.]

[1]: If you are invisible, light passes through you. If light passes
through you, it is not absorbed by your retinas. If light is not
absorbed by your retinas, you can't see. --azgor

[2]: "You attempt to light the cursed lamp. Ouch! You burnt your
<finger>!" (With fireres: "The flame plays harmlessly over your
<finger> before going out." --GreyKnight

[3]: Even if you don't identify a loadstone as cursed while holding
and pray when stressed, your God should FUCKING UNCURSE IT ANYWAY.
 --aristotle73

[4]: Since Mjollnir (and bolts of lightning) can destroy rings on
targets, destroying a Nazgul's ring should have some effect.
(instakill?)  --Grunt

[5]: Orcs and leprechauns should hate each other for the gold. --Grunt

[6]: A 'statue coming to life' should be different for golems: The
gold piece/glass piece/unlabeled scroll/rock comes to life,
depending on the type of golem. --HappyFoppy

[7]: Cursed kicking boots should prevent you from kicking things.
("These boots feel like concrete shoes!") --Grunt

[8]: Potions of Oil should behave as potions of healing when quaffed
by an Iron Golem. --aristotle73

[9]: Leprechauns should do massive damage to gold golems.  (Hehe.)
--Grunt

[10]: Really break the wand of light? You break the wand of light!
You get a tan! You feel better looking. (Charisma +1) --offipso

[11]: Brass knuckles for those geared towards unarmed combat, can be 
enchanted to yield regular damage and accuracy boni. Those 
fashion(in)sensitive could also accessorize with silver knuckles
for that night out in Gehennom. --alphamale

[12]: Reading a confused blessed scroll of enchant weapon while
wielding a +5 quarterstaff in one hand and a dilithium crystal
in the other will cause the dilithium crystal to be embedded in
the staff giving it magical properties (for example, being able
to zap lightning, fire, or cold from the staff).  The
quarterstaff will be self charging, possesing a charge of 0:1.
  Once zapped, its charge becomes 0:0 and the player must wait
several hundred turns for the staff to recharge itself before 
zapping again.  Different types of dilithium crystals can imbue
different spell types but only one crystal per staff can be used.
Attempting to read a confused blessed scroll of enchant weapon
with an already magically powered staff causes one of two events
based on luck: 1:  "There is a loud whine as the staff glows black.
The foo dillithium crystal shatters!"  2:  "The staff begins to 
splinter.  It explodes!" Only wizards can create magical staves
and only they can identify them without zapping or engraving with
the staff.  Attempting to do this as a non-wizard gives the message
"You think the staff shivered." Nothing will happen.  Types of
crystals: green (regeneration), black (death), orange (fire), blue
(lightning), white (cold), silver (protection).  Imbuing the magic
of a black dillithium crystal into a staff while wearing a cursed
ring of hunger disintergrates the ring and gives the staff Drain
Life. This drains HP from an enemy and gives it to the wielder
upon striking.  It possesses no charges. --aristotle73

